It has the highest execution certainty, and every stage number reproduces today. I reran habit.py and fix.py:
- $20.06 vs $58.41 per MW-day, which is $1,405 vs $4,088 a day at 70 MW;
- -18.4 t vs +18.9 t CO2 a day;
- $14,496-17,708 per MW-year;
- a 3.4% cost for a battery-only reserve.
The Oct 27 price figures also check out against the snapshot CSV: $38.71 overnight vs $22.83 midday, and a 3,655 MW net-load climb from 3pm to 6pm. The engine is static and in-browser, so nothing on the stage path needs the network. 'A battery is only as clean as the hour it charges' is the clearest line in the field. It uses the CTO's own freeway metaphor and matches the research's recommended Option 1 spine almost exactly.
